## Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a card which flips (rotates) around the Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣  Container ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  perspective: 1000px;          /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
  margin: 50px auto;            /* center horizontally */
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣  Card (the element that will rotate) ---------- */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;  /* keep children in 3D space */
  transition: transform 0.8s ease; /* smooth animation */
}

/* Hover triggers the rotation */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣  Front & Back faces ---------- */
.card-face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* hide the back side when facing away */
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
}

/* Front face */
.card-front {
  background: #f5f5f5;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #333;
}

/* Back face – rotated 180° so it starts hidden */
.card-back {
  background: #4a90e2;
  color: #fff;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* start flipped */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-face card-front">
      Front Side
    </div>
    <div class="card-face card-back">
      Back Side
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | CSS property |
|------|--------------|--------------|
| 1 | The wrapper gives the card a 3D context (`perspective`). | `perspective: 1000px;` |
| 2 | The `.card` element is set to preserve its children in 3D (`transform-style: preserve-3d`) and has a transition for smooth rotation. | `transform-style: preserve-3d;`<br>`transition: transform 0.8s ease;` |
| 3 | On hover, the card rotates 180° around the Y‑axis. | `transform: rotateY(180deg);` |
| 4 | Each face (`.card-face`) is absolutely positioned, covers the whole card, and hides its back side when not visible (`backface-visibility: hidden`). | `backface-visibility: hidden;` |
| 5 | The back face is initially rotated 180° so that it is hidden until the card flips. | `transform: rotateY(180deg);` |

Feel free to replace the text, colors, or add more content inside the faces.  
If you want a flip around the X‑axis instead, just change `rotateY` to `rotateX`.
